# Reg Barclay, Fidgety Fantasist: "Seek out -- Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a token that's a copy
# of another target creature you control, except it isn't legendary, it's an Illusion artifact in addition to its other
# types, and it has haste. Exile that token at the beginning of the next end step." (CR 603.2, 121.2, 707.2, 603.7c).
#
# Bot1 casts it on turn 1 for {2}{U}{R} off a Black Lotus and a Mox Ruby, then Isamaru, Hound of Konda off a Mox Pearl
# and a free Memnite (the pool checked empty). Bot2 has a Llanowar Elves. On turn 5 the draw step's card is the turn's
# first and Consider draws the second, so the trigger asks for its target: Reg Barclay itself is not "another" and
# Bot2's Elves are not "you control", both refused, and it takes the legendary Isamaru. The token is a hasty 2/2 that
# stands beside the legend - it is not legendary (CR 707.2), and it is an Illusion artifact as well as a Dog creature
# (CR 707.9b), while the original stays a plain Dog creature - and at the beginning of that turn's end step it is exiled.

